// ⚠️  DROP-IN FIREBASE IMPLEMENTATION — NOT COMPILED BY DEFAULT ⚠️
//
// The app ships with a no-op `LocalOnlyCloudSyncService` so it builds and runs
// with zero Firebase configuration. To enable cloud backup & sync for Pro users:
//
//   1. Add the Firebase dependencies:
//        flutter pub add firebase_core firebase_auth cloud_firestore google_sign_in
//   2. Run `flutterfire configure` (adds android/app/google-services.json and
//      lib/firebase_options.dart) and apply the google-services Gradle plugin
//      (see README → "Firebase setup").
//   3. Rename this file to `firebase_cloud_sync_service.dart`.
//   4. In `lib/main.dart`, initialise Firebase before runApp:
//        await Firebase.initializeApp(
//            options: DefaultFirebaseOptions.currentPlatform);
//        // sign in anonymously so every user has a stable uid:
//        await FirebaseAuth.instance.signInAnonymously();
//   5. Override the provider in your ProviderScope:
//        cloudSyncServiceProvider.overrideWithValue(FirebaseCloudSyncService()),
//
// Firestore layout (matches the security rules in the README):
//   users/{uid}/scans/{recordId}  ->  ScanRecord.toJson()
